            {
              "id": "cc8.1/emergency-change",
              "name": "EmergencyChange",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Emergency change process is documented"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An emergency (hotfix / break-glass) change process is documented, including who may use it and the retroactive review it requires."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Document the emergency change path: who can invoke it, what is skipped, and the retroactive review required within a set time.\n\nRisk: Without a defined path, urgent fixes bypass review informally and leave no audit trail, which auditors treat as a control failure.",
                "markdown": "**CC8.1**: An emergency (hotfix / break-glass) change process is documented, including who may use it and the retroactive review it requires.\n\n**Risk:** Without a defined path, urgent fixes bypass review informally and leave no audit trail, which auditors treat as a control failure.\n\n**Fix:** Document the emergency change path: who can invoke it, what is skipped, and the retroactive review required within a set time.\n\nExample:\n\n```\n## Emergency changes\nUse only for active incidents. An on-call engineer may merge with one approval from the incident commander.\nA retroactive review PR is opened within 2 business days and linked from the incident ticket.\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
