            {
              "id": "cc8.1/migrations-reversible",
              "name": "MigrationsReversible",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Database migrations are reversible or have a rollback plan"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Each migration has a down/downgrade step, or the repository documents how schema changes are rolled back."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Write a down migration for each change, or document the expand/contract and restore procedure used instead.\n\nRisk: A bad migration without a way back turns a deploy rollback into a data-recovery incident.",
                "markdown": "**CC8.1**: Each migration has a down/downgrade step, or the repository documents how schema changes are rolled back.\n\n**Risk:** A bad migration without a way back turns a deploy rollback into a data-recovery incident.\n\n**Fix:** Write a down migration for each change, or document the expand/contract and restore procedure used instead.\n\nExample:\n\n```\n-- 20261022_add_status.down.sql\nALTER TABLE orders DROP COLUMN status;\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
