            {
              "id": "cc8.1/rollback-procedure",
              "name": "RollbackProcedure",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Rollback procedure is documented"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A runbook explains how to roll back a bad release, who can do it, and how to verify it worked."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Add a rollback section to your deployment runbook (docs/runbooks/rollback.md) and rehearse it.\n\nRisk: Under incident pressure, an undocumented rollback is slow, inconsistent and easy to get wrong.",
                "markdown": "**CC8.1**: A runbook explains how to roll back a bad release, who can do it, and how to verify it worked.\n\n**Risk:** Under incident pressure, an undocumented rollback is slow, inconsistent and easy to get wrong.\n\n**Fix:** Add a rollback section to your deployment runbook (docs/runbooks/rollback.md) and rehearse it.\n\nExample:\n\n```\n## Rolling back a release\n1. Find the last good deployment in the Deployments tab.\n2. Promote it: `vercel promote <deployment-url>` (or re-run the deploy workflow for the previous tag).\n3. Confirm health checks and error rates recover; post in #incidents.\n```"
              },
