            {
              "id": "cc8.1/terraform-state",
              "name": "TerraformState",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Terraform state is remote, locked and not committed"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Terraform state lives in a remote, locked, access-controlled backend, and state files are never committed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Configure a remote backend with locking, remove committed state from git (and rotate any secrets it held), and gitignore *.tfstate.\n\nRisk: State files contain secrets in plain text, and unlocked or local state lets concurrent applies corrupt infrastructure.",
                "markdown": "**CC8.1**: Terraform state lives in a remote, locked, access-controlled backend, and state files are never committed.\n\n**Risk:** State files contain secrets in plain text, and unlocked or local state lets concurrent applies corrupt infrastructure.\n\n**Fix:** Configure a remote backend with locking, remove committed state from git (and rotate any secrets it held), and gitignore *.tfstate.\n\nExample:\n\n```\nterraform {\n  backend \"s3\" {\n    bucket       = \"acme-terraform-state\"\n    key          = \"prod/terraform.tfstate\"\n    region       = \"us-east-1\"\n    encrypt      = true\n    use_lockfile = true\n  }\n}\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
