                "criterion": "PI1.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "pi1.2/input-validation",
              "name": "InputValidation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Inputs are validated against schemas at the trust boundary"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Request bodies, query parameters and webhook payloads are validated server-side with a schema library."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Validate every request with a schema (Zod, Pydantic, Joi, validator) and reject what does not match.\n\nRisk: Unvalidated input causes silent data corruption, crashes and injection, and lets clients send totals or IDs the server should compute.",
                "markdown": "**PI1.2**: Request bodies, query parameters and webhook payloads are validated server-side with a schema library.\n\n**Risk:** Unvalidated input causes silent data corruption, crashes and injection, and lets clients send totals or IDs the server should compute.\n\n**Fix:** Validate every request with a schema (Zod, Pydantic, Joi, validator) and reject what does not match.\n\nExample:\n\n```\nconst Order = z.object({ sku: z.string().min(1), quantity: z.number().int().positive().max(100) });\nconst order = Order.parse(req.body);\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "soc2",
                  "PI1.2"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "criterion": "PI1.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "pi1.3/job-retries",
              "name": "JobRetries",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Background jobs have bounded retries and a dead-letter path"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Jobs and consumers set retry limits with backoff, and failed work lands in a dead-letter queue that is monitored."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Configure attempts and backoff on every queue, and route exhausted messages to a dead-letter queue.\n\nRisk: Failed jobs are dropped silently or retried forever, losing or duplicating work.",
                "markdown": "**PI1.3**: Jobs and consumers set retry limits with backoff, and failed work lands in a dead-letter queue that is monitored.\n\n**Risk:** Failed jobs are dropped silently or retried forever, losing or duplicating work.\n\n**Fix:** Configure attempts and backoff on every queue, and route exhausted messages to a dead-letter queue.\n\nExample:\n\n```\nawait queue.add('send-invoice', data, { attempts: 5, backoff: { type: 'exponential', delay: 1000 } });\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "soc2",
                  "PI1.3"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "criterion": "PI1.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "pi1.5/db-constraints",
              "name": "DbConstraints",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Database schemas enforce integrity constraints"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Schemas declare NOT NULL, UNIQUE, foreign key and check constraints, so the database rejects invalid data even when application code misses it."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare constraints in the schema for required fields, uniqueness and relationships.\n\nRisk: Without constraints, a single bug writes orphaned or duplicate records that corrupt reports and billing.",
                "markdown": "**PI1.5**: Schemas declare NOT NULL, UNIQUE, foreign key and check constraints, so the database rejects invalid data even when application code misses it.\n\n**Risk:** Without constraints, a single bug writes orphaned or duplicate records that corrupt reports and billing.\n\n**Fix:** Declare constraints in the schema for required fields, uniqueness and relationships.\n\nExample:\n\n```\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY,\n  customer_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES customers(id),\n  total_cents integer NOT NULL CHECK (total_cents >= 0)\n);\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "soc2",
                  "PI1.5"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "criterion": "PI1.5"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
